  data:  # f27d
    kind: invariant  # f27d
    title: "Linker-synthesized Symbols missing origin stamp across 19 of 21 linker files (only message_queue + database_query stamp correctly)"  # f27d
    status: violated  # f27d
    priority: 2  # f27d
    parent:  # f27d
    tags:  # f27d
    - self_analysis  # f27d
    - dogfooding  # f27d
    - adr_0014  # f27d
    isbefore: []  # f27d
    duplicate_of: []  # f27d
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f27d
    pr_ref:  # f27d
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 2).**\n\n**Symptom.** Hypergumbo's own self-analysis surfaces 95 Symbol nodes with empty `origin` field — 18 `function` nodes with route-handler names (`GET /api/users`, `DELETE /api/users/1`, `GET event.request`) and 77 `call_site` nodes with subprocess-command names (`app1 cmd1`, `git add`, `app2 cmd2`).\n\n**True scope.** Investigation found that this is not 2 bugs but a class of bugs across **19 of 21 linker files**. Each linker correctly defines a `PASS_ID = make_pass_id(\"<name>\")` constant and uses it to stamp `Edge.origin` on emitted edges, but the parallel pattern for `Symbol.origin` on linker-synthesized symbols is omitted in 19 of 21 cases.\n\n**Files affected (Symbol-origin omitted):**\n\n`annotation_convention`, `crypto_flow`, `graphql`, `grpc`, `http`, `ipc`, `js_module`, `message_dispatch`, `openapi`, `phoenix_ipc`, `solidity_abi`, `subprocess_cli`, `swift_objc`, `tauri_ipc`, `_view_template_core`, `vue_component`, `wasm_bindgen`, `websocket`, `yjs_crdt`.\n\n**Files that do it correctly (positive contrast):**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/message_queue.py:466-470` — stamps `symbol.origin = PASS_ID` + `symbol.origin_run_id = run.execution_id` after construction\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/database_query.py:413-414` — same idiom\n\n**Confirmed source-locus examples:**\n\n- `linkers/http.py:1319-1347` — `_create_client_symbol(call, root)` constructs `Symbol(...)` without `origin=PASS_ID`. PASS_ID (`\"http-linker-v1\"`) defined at line 102 and used for Edge.origin at line 1490 — asymmetric.\n- `linkers/subprocess_cli.py:312-342` — `_create_call_symbol(call, root)` same pattern. PASS_ID (`\"subprocess-linker-v1\"`) defined at line 58, used for Edge.origin at line 444.\n\n**Invariant.** Every Symbol emitted by an analyzer or linker MUST carry a non-empty `origin` field matching the producer's versioned PASS_ID. Compare with `Symbol.origin` docstring at `ir.py:204-359`: \"For analyzer-emitted symbols, this SHOULD be a versioned analyzer ID such as `python-v1`, `go-v1`, etc.\" — the same rule applies to linker-emitted synthesis symbols.\n\n**Two fix paths.**\n\n1. **19-file copy-paste of the `message_queue.py:466-470` stamp idiom.** Lowest semantic risk; tedious; doesn't catch future regressions when a 22nd linker is added.\n\n2. **Make `origin` a required kwarg on `Symbol.__init__`.** Structural fix per ADR-0024 axis-declaration discipline — promotes the rule from a convention to an enforced invariant. Catches all 19 current sites and any future linker that forgets to stamp. The transitional path: keep `origin` as optional with a deprecation warning + linter check, then flip to required in a later release.\n\nRecommended: (2) for the structural fix, with (1) as the immediate unblock if shipping (2) is too invasive in one PR. Approach (1) alone closes the current symptom but leaves the invariant unenforced.\n\n**Test gap.** None of the affected linkers' tests assert `sym.origin == \"<pass_id>\"` on synthesized Symbols. Example: `packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_http_linker.py::TestCreateClientSymbolStableId` (lines 1827-1897) exercises `_create_client_symbol` six times and asserts `stable_id` / `id` but never `sym.origin`. Each affected linker needs at least one origin-stamp assertion.\n\n**Why nodes have empty `origin_run_id` too.** Same omission. The `message_queue.py` precedent shows BOTH need to be stamped: `symbol.origin = PASS_ID; symbol.origin_run_id = run.execution_id`. The bug is symmetric across the two provenance fields.\n\n**Downstream consequence.** Mixed-fidelity analysis cannot filter or weight linker-synthesized symbols by producer trust. Self-analysis cohorts that group by `origin` (e.g., \"which analyzer/linker produced what?\") undercount these 19 linkers' contributions. The IR docstring's own concept-leak documentation (re: synthesis-origin field split into `synthesis_mechanism`) compounds with this: external_symbol nodes also have empty origin (intentionally, per the documented exception). The result is two distinct empty-origin populations — synthesized-by-linker (this bug) vs synthesized-as-boundary (concept leak) — indistinguishable downstream.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py:204-359` (Symbol docstring)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/message_queue.py:466-470` (correct precedent)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/database_query.py:413-414` (correct precedent)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/http.py:102, 1319-1347, 1415-1416, 1490` (one affected example with PASS_ID at 102)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/subprocess_cli.py:58, 312-342, 391-392, 444` (second affected example)"  # f27d
    fields:  # f27d
      statement: "Every Symbol emitted by an analyzer or linker MUST carry a non-empty origin field matching the producer's versioned PASS_ID. The same convention that holds for analyzer-emitted symbols (python-v1, go-v1, etc., per Symbol docstring at ir.py:204-359) extends to linker-emitted synthesis symbols."  # f27d
      root_cause: "Each affected linker correctly defines PASS_ID = make_pass_id('<name>') and uses it to stamp Edge.origin on emitted edges, but the parallel post-construction stamp on Symbol.origin (and Symbol.origin_run_id) is omitted in 19 of 21 linker files. Only linkers/message_queue.py:466-470 and linkers/database_query.py:413-414 do it correctly. Affected: annotation_convention, crypto_flow, graphql, grpc, http, ipc, js_module, message_dispatch, openapi, phoenix_ipc, solidity_abi, subprocess_cli, swift_objc, tauri_ipc, _view_template_core, vue_component, wasm_bindgen, websocket, yjs_crdt."  # f27d
